ROUTE DECISIONS
===============
D-001 | Use GitHub issue #39 as human claim/event surface and docs/coordination/tasks.json as machine-readable task source. Reason: agents need both easy comments and deterministic repository state.
D-002 | Keep handoff.md small and index-oriented; detailed history belongs in logs/issues/docs. Reason: handoff is parsed/read on every join and must stay fast.
D-003 | Current product route is release hardening, not feature expansion. Highest priorities after bootstrap: finish PR #38 audit, signer identity binding, revocation policy, and branch governance.
D-004 | Because C0/A0/W0 are the same ChatGPT during bootstrap, self-review is allowed only with role separation: worker commits first, auditor re-fetches GitHub evidence independently, coordinator then records decision.
D-005 | Do not merge coordination bootstrap directly to main; open a PR and run audit first.
D-006 | Redundant coordination Issues are harmful because they look like separate work queues. Keep one canonical channel per coordination function; close informational duplicates once durable docs exist.
D-007 | HLS-C001 implementation may continue in parallel, but its merge is blocked until PR #38/HLS-C002 fixes the exact-main-SHA workflow availability contract. Reason: a docs-only bootstrap merge on old main could make formal release impossible for the current SHA.
D-008 | Formal-release exact-SHA gates and workflow trigger coverage are one contract. If a workflow is required for every release SHA, its main-push trigger must also exist for every main SHA; do not solve only the consumer side.
